  "settings": [
    {
      "zh": "Regular车壳至少240×150mm平台；官方Ultimaker S5样例：0.2mm层高、1.5mm壁厚、20% grid、80mm/s、无支撑。PLA/ABS/CPE曾用于原作者试印。不是其他打印机的保证。",
      "en": "Regular body requires at least 240×150mm. Source Ultimaker S5 example: 0.2mm layer, 1.5mm wall, 20% grid, 80mm/s, no support; author used PLA/ABS/CPE. Not a guarantee for other printers."
    }
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Step 01",
      "text": {
        "zh": "Solder wires to the motors and add the encoder disks to the two front motors if you intend to use the speed sensors.",
        "en": "Solder wires to the motors and add the encoder disks to the two front motors if you intend to use the speed sensors."
      },
      "source": "https://github.com/ob-f/OpenBot/blob/db044a7d2e50d204cf6e6f9dc80492a484ad5441/body/diy/README.md#option-1-diy"
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 02",
      "text": {
        "zh": "Insert the positive and negative leads of the two left motors into OUT1 (+) and OUT2 (-) of the L298N board. Insert the positive and negative leads of the two right motors into OUT4 (+) and OUT3 (-) of the L298N board.",
        "en": "Insert the positive and negative leads of the two left motors into OUT1 (+) and OUT2 (-) of the L298N board. Insert the positive and negative leads of the two right motors into OUT4 (+) and OUT3 (-) of the L298N board."
      },
      "source": "https://github.com/ob-f/OpenBot/blob/db044a7d2e50d204cf6e6f9dc80492a484ad5441/body/diy/README.md#option-1-diy"
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 03",
      "text": {
        "zh": "Mount the motors with eight M3x25 screws and nuts.",
        "en": "Mount the motors with eight M3x25 screws and nuts."
      },
      "source": "https://github.com/ob-f/OpenBot/blob/db044a7d2e50d204cf6e6f9dc80492a484ad5441/body/diy/README.md#option-1-diy"
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 04",
      "text": {
        "zh": "Mount the L298N with four M3x5 screws",
        "en": "Mount the L298N with four M3x5 screws"
      },
      "source": "https://github.com/ob-f/OpenBot/blob/db044a7d2e50d204cf6e6f9dc80492a484ad5441/body/diy/README.md#option-1-diy"
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 05",
      "text": {
        "zh": "(Optional) Install the ultrasonic sensor and replace the angled connector with a straigt one (or carefully bend the pins).",
        "en": "(Optional) Install the ultrasonic sensor and replace the angled connector with a straigt one (or carefully bend the pins)."
      },
      "source": "https://github.com/ob-f/OpenBot/blob/db044a7d2e50d204cf6e6f9dc80492a484ad5441/body/diy/README.md#option-1-diy"
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 06",
      "text": {
        "zh": "(Optional) Install the orange LEDs for the indicator signals.",
        "en": "(Optional) Install the orange LEDs for the indicator signals."
      },
      "source": "https://github.com/ob-f/OpenBot/blob/db044a7d2e50d204cf6e6f9dc80492a484ad5441/body/diy/README.md#option-1-diy"
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 07",
      "text": {
        "zh": "Mount the bottom of the phone mount to the top plate using two M3x25 screws and nuts.",
        "en": "Mount the bottom of the phone mount to the top plate using two M3x25 screws and nuts."
      },
      "source": "https://github.com/ob-f/OpenBot/blob/db044a7d2e50d204cf6e6f9dc80492a484ad5441/body/diy/README.md#option-1-diy"
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 08",
      "text": {
        "zh": "Insert the top of the phone mount and install the spring or rubber band.",
        "en": "Insert the top of the phone mount and install the spring or rubber band."
      },
      "source": "https://github.com/ob-f/OpenBot/blob/db044a7d2e50d204cf6e6f9dc80492a484ad5441/body/diy/README.md#option-1-diy"
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 09",
      "text": {
        "zh": "Replace the angled connector with a straigt one (or carefully bend the pins) and then mount the speed sensors with one M3x5 screw each.",
        "en": "Replace the angled connector with a straigt one (or carefully bend the pins) and then mount the speed sensors with one M3x5 screw each."
      },
      "source": "https://github.com/ob-f/OpenBot/blob/db044a7d2e50d204cf6e6f9dc80492a484ad5441/body/diy/README.md#option-1-diy"
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 10",
      "text": {
        "zh": "Install the battery case (e.g. velcro).",
        "en": "Install the battery case (e.g. velcro)."
      },
      "source": "https://github.com/ob-f/OpenBot/blob/db044a7d2e50d204cf6e6f9dc80492a484ad5441/body/diy/README.md#option-1-diy"
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 11",
      "text": {
        "zh": "(Optional) Insert the on/off switch put it in the current path.",
        "en": "(Optional) Insert the on/off switch put it in the current path."
      },
      "source": "https://github.com/ob-f/OpenBot/blob/db044a7d2e50d204cf6e6f9dc80492a484ad5441/body/diy/README.md#option-1-diy"
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 12",
      "text": {
        "zh": "(Optional) Attach the OLED display.",
        "en": "(Optional) Attach the OLED display."
      },
      "source": "https://github.com/ob-f/OpenBot/blob/db044a7d2e50d204cf6e6f9dc80492a484ad5441/body/diy/README.md#option-1-diy"
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 13",
      "text": {
        "zh": "Connect the PWM inputs of the L298N to pins D5, D6, D9 and D10 of the Arduino.",
        "en": "Connect the PWM inputs of the L298N to pins D5, D6, D9 and D10 of the Arduino."
      },
      "source": "https://github.com/ob-f/OpenBot/blob/db044a7d2e50d204cf6e6f9dc80492a484ad5441/body/diy/README.md#option-1-diy"
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 14",
      "text": {
        "zh": "Connect the speed sensors and ultrasonic sensor to 5V and GND.",
        "en": "Connect the speed sensors and ultrasonic sensor to 5V and GND."
      },
      "source": "https://github.com/ob-f/OpenBot/blob/db044a7d2e50d204cf6e6f9dc80492a484ad5441/body/diy/README.md#option-1-diy"
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 15",
      "text": {
        "zh": "Connect pin D0 of the speed sensors to pins D2 (left) and D3 (right) of the Arduino.",
        "en": "Connect pin D0 of the speed sensors to pins D2 (left) and D3 (right) of the Arduino."
      },
      "source": "https://github.com/ob-f/OpenBot/blob/db044a7d2e50d204cf6e6f9dc80492a484ad5441/body/diy/README.md#option-1-diy"
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 16",
      "text": {
        "zh": "Connect pins Echo and Trigger of the ultrasonic sensor to pins D11 and D12 of the Arduino respectively.",
        "en": "Connect pins Echo and Trigger of the ultrasonic sensor to pins D11 and D12 of the Arduino respectively."
      },
      "source": "https://github.com/ob-f/OpenBot/blob/db044a7d2e50d204cf6e6f9dc80492a484ad5441/body/diy/README.md#option-1-diy"
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 17",
      "text": {
        "zh": "(Optional) Connect the LEDs to pins D4 (left) and D7 (right) of the Arduino and GND. We recommend to add a 150 Ohm resistor in series to limit the current draw.",
        "en": "(Optional) Connect the LEDs to pins D4 (left) and D7 (right) of the Arduino and GND. We recommend to add a 150 Ohm resistor in series to limit the current draw."
      },
      "source": "https://github.com/ob-f/OpenBot/blob/db044a7d2e50d204cf6e6f9dc80492a484ad5441/body/diy/README.md#option-1-diy"
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 18",
      "text": {
        "zh": "(Optional) Connect the voltage divider to pin A7 of the Arduino. It is used to measure the battery voltage.",
        "en": "(Optional) Connect the voltage divider to pin A7 of the Arduino. It is used to measure the battery voltage."
      },
      "source": "https://github.com/ob-f/OpenBot/blob/db044a7d2e50d204cf6e6f9dc80492a484ad5441/body/diy/README.md#option-1-diy"
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 19",
      "text": {
        "zh": "(Optional) Connect the OLED display (SSD1306 chip) via the I2C bus to the Arduino Nano",
        "en": "(Optional) Connect the OLED display (SSD1306 chip) via the I2C bus to the Arduino Nano"
      },
      "source": "https://github.com/ob-f/OpenBot/blob/db044a7d2e50d204cf6e6f9dc80492a484ad5441/body/diy/README.md#option-1-diy"
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 20",
      "text": {
        "zh": "Connect the power cables to +12V and GND of the L298N.",
        "en": "Connect the power cables to +12V and GND of the L298N."
      },
      "source": "https://github.com/ob-f/OpenBot/blob/db044a7d2e50d204cf6e6f9dc80492a484ad5441/body/diy/README.md#option-1-diy"
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 21",
      "text": {
        "zh": "Connect the USB cable to the Arduino and route it through the top cover.",
        "en": "Connect the USB cable to the Arduino and route it through the top cover."
      },
      "source": "https://github.com/ob-f/OpenBot/blob/db044a7d2e50d204cf6e6f9dc80492a484ad5441/body/diy/README.md#option-1-diy"
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 22",
      "text": {
